569 0 obj
<<
/A 4406 0 R
/Alt (Line graph with discrimination threshold along horizontal x-axis, from 0.0 to 1.0 in 0.1 increments and tick marks at 0.02, and score on vertical y-axis, from 0.0 to 1.0 in 0.2 increments and horizontal grid line at every 0.1. There are three lines: green solid line for F1, bright blue dashed line for precision, and red short-dashed line for recall. The green solid F1 line starts from 0.20, quickly rises to 0.50, drops to a score of about 0.40 at about a 0.3 discrimination threshold, remains at about this score until about a 0.8 discrimination threshold after which it drops and ends at 0.30. The bright blue dashed precision line starts at zero, quickly rises to 0.4, remains at this score until it starts slowly rising at about a 0.60 discrimination threshold, reaches 0.5 at a discrimination threshold of about 0.80, dips to about 0.45 shortly thereafter and remains at this level until the end where it rises to 0.47. The red short-dashed recall line starts at 1.0, concavely drops to 0.4 by a discrimination threshold of about 0.35, remains near this score until a discrimination threshold of about 0.55 by which it has dropped to a score of 0.35, maintains and then starts to decrease at a discrimination threshold of about 0.75, and ends at a score of about 0.23. A vertical dotted line extends at the 0.5 discrimination threshold to identify the threshold used in the analysis.␀)
/ID (AD000000-0000-0000-ADBE-      121054)
/K 1
